Leave CARGO_HOME to the environment.

Arch's PKGBUILD points CARGO_HOME at $srcdir so the fetch stays inside the
build tree. On the farm the sourcer captures prepare()'s fetch into the
source package through CARGO_HOME, and the worker replays it offline the
same way; this export overrides both, so the crates land in a tree that is
thrown away and the offline build has nothing to fetch from. With it gone
the fetch goes to cargo's registry cache as for every other Rust package.

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@
 _srcenv() {
 	cd "$_archive"
-	export CARGO_HOME="$srcdir"
 	export CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=2
 	export CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP=false
 	export CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO=true
